5. The reasoning agent should put more emphasis on avoiding conflicts with high-importance calendar events, especially when considering flights on the same day as these events.

6. The action agent should be more responsive to the different flight combinations suggested by the reasoning agent, rather than defaulting to the same choice repeatedly.

Moving forward, both the reasoning and action agents should prioritize finding flight combinations that avoid conflicts with important calendar events while still maintaining cost-effectiveness. They should also explore a wider range of options throughout the iterations to increase the likelihood of finding an optimal solution for both users.
