2. Action Agent: Based on the reasoning, select the best flight options for each user that adhere to the prioritized rules. Ensure that the chosen flights do not conflict with high-importance calendar events, have competitive prices, and arrive relatively close to each other.

3. Reflection Agent: Evaluate the selected flights against the given rules and user requirements. Confirm that the choices respect important calendar events, offer good value, and minimize arrival time differences. If any improvements can be made, suggest them for reconsideration.

Remember, the priority of rules is: calendar conflicts (most important), price, and arrival time difference (least important). Your decisions should reflect this order of importance.
